{"kind":"report","text":"Resolved without a code change: the reported parent-path pull is intentional merge coverage, not a succession-scoping defect.\n\nThe exact-string rule and the coverage rule are distinct. SKILL.md says artifact paths are exact wires for provenance and succession identity—internal/service never becomes the same artifact path as internal/service/uidist—but then explicitly requires every live artifact covering a changed file to be accounted for and says that when a directory and something inside it are both live over one changed file, the wider path wins. docs/reference/gs/merge.md states the same enforced result. In code, cmd/gs/succession.go's covering/artifactCoversPath logic identifies directory coverage and widest selects the stable successor path. The prospective cross-author guard then deliberately reads reviewed reach only downward, never upward: a review of internal/service/uidist cannot authorize retirement of another actor's internal/service pointer. That is the safety property producing the refusal.\n\nThe b7310bf4 head changes committed files beneath internal/service/uidist, so it also changes the wider maintained internal/service directory state. Publishing a candidate artifact at internal/service therefore does not claim that internal/service/*.go changed; it truthfully says the directory's reviewed exact head differs through the nested generated bundle.\n\nExact clean unblock: Claude publishes an implementer-owned artifact at exact path internal/service for unchanged head 1b453fea2ce30b1d2d6d773234d939c9cd79d6b1, describing that limited nested change; then requests fresh independent review naming ui, internal/service/uidist, and internal/service. The reviewer records A/S/S against the unchanged exact head and signs all three artifact paths; Claude ratifies; the original requester authorizes that exact head and complete set; gs merge then performs the parent and nested succession atomically. Do not hand-retire the four parent artifacts and do not merely widen authorization around an approval that never cited the parent path.\n\nThe same rule confirms identity follow-up faefb6b0 is necessary: exact head 2a616a74 changes host/identity under live parent path host, so the fresh review must cite host + host/identity + architecture before merge.\n\nIndependent focused evidence passed on current main: TestMergeWiderPathWinsOverNestedArtifact, TestMergePreflightRefusesACrossAuthorRetirementOutsideTheApprovedTree, TestMergeResumeAppendsASealedSymmetricReceiptWithoutReplanningOrRemerging, and the broader focused cmd/gs succession set. The assigned worktree is clean; no files, commits, or merge behavior were changed. Please ratify this report and retire request 230abf26 as resolved by the documented contract.","body":{"head":"3f35d6edf4d0d81002ed1c3dab6d7e80ba27c0f5"}}